   ],
   "rect": {
    "x": 960,
    "y": 3030,
    "w": 180,
    "h": 180
   }
  },
  {
   "file": "yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7",
   "alt": "There was a time when writing in a diary was seen as the domain of teenage girls. It was supposed to be this book covered in pink and purple, where they jotted down the pains and pleasures of adolescence. It was seen as more of a fad, to be buried as soon as ‘real life’ set in. However, diary-writing or journaling has seen a surge in popularity in recent times. Today, it is considered as an important and effective tool in dealing with problems and helping in improving overall quality of life.⠀\n⠀\nHave you found the treasures of journaling?⠀\n⠀\nRead the latest post on the blog. Link in bio.",
   "natural": [
    1,
    1
   ],
   "rect": {
    "x": 97,
    "y": 5215,
    "w": 1,
    "h": 1
   }
  },
  {
   "file": "yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7",
   "alt": "How often we get bogged down with the non-essentials. Too often we allow the imposter syndrome to keep us from being successful. Fear. Anxiety. Lack of motivation. Lack of discipline. These are just some of the things that keep us from being the best writers we can be. Remember that YOU are the creator of your writing. True, you are inspired by various people, events and sources, but the bottom line is that YOU are in control. It’s important then to stay true to yourself. To write authentically. To be fearless. Today, I’m sharing with you some quotes to encourage you to be a fearless writer.⠀\nBe a fearless writer! Write bravely!\n\nLink in bio.",
   "natural": [
    1,
    1
   ],
   "rect": {
    "x": 97,
    "y": 5303,
    "w": 1,
    "h": 1
   }
  },
  {
   "file": "yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7",
   "alt": "Looking back is only good when you are taking stock. But looking back with regrets serves no useful purpose.\nLook back to see how far you've come. Take stock of your gifts, your failures because the lessons you've learnt through them, your achievements because of the strength you experienced in them, and look within at the untapped potential in you!\nToday, celebrate You!",
   "natural": [
    1,
    1
   ],
   "rect": {
    "x": 97,
    "y": 5391,
    "w": 1,
    "h": 1
   }
  },
  {
   "file": "yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7",
   "alt": "A couple of months ago, I was so excited to buy this from @paperquirkstationery . Have been using the ruler and pencils, but have been reluctant to start writing in this fancy notebook. That's going to change today.\nDo you you also hoard stationery and keep good notebooks for the day your writing is perfect?\nLet's enjoy being creative and stop waiting to be perfect!!",
   "natural": [
    1,
    1
   ],
   "rect": {
    "x": 97,
    "y": 5479,
    "w": 1,
    "h": 1
   }
  },
  {
   "file": "yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7",
   "alt": "How do you tackle your inner critic - that voice in your head that keeps questioning your creativity, urges you to compare yourself with others and sometimes results in creativity paralysis.\nListen to episode 3 of The Frangipani Creative podcast on how to tackle your inner critic.\n\nLink in bio.",
   "natural": [
    1,
    1
   ],
   "rect": {
    "x": 97,
    "y": 5566,
    "w": 1,
    "h": 1
   }
  },
  {
   "file": "yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7",
   "alt": "We have the capacity for infinite creativity. - Jackie Gleason\nListen to Episode 2 of The Frangipani Creative podcast.\nLink in bio.",
   "natural": [
    1,
    1
   ],
   "rect": {
    "x": 97,
    "y": 5654,
    "w": 1,
    "h": 1
   }
  },
  {
   "file": "yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7",
   "alt": "Are you working on something right now and getting upset with yourself because progress is slow? Remember, we're living in unprecedented times. Times when survival is paramount. Adding the stress of deadlines and goals could be counter productive! \nBe kind to yourself!",
   "natural": [
    1,
    1
   ],
